  "basis": "The state risk dashboard uses a color scale where lighter shades (yellow) indicate lower risk (0) and darker shades (red/burgundy) indicate higher risk (100). The legend explicitly maps 'Low' at 0 to dark burgundy and 'High' at 100 to pale yellow. Utah (UT) is colored very pale yellow, indicating the lowest risk. Delaware (DE) is colored light orange, indicating a medium risk. Vermont (VT) is colored dark burgundy, indicating the highest risk. Under the routing criterion to select the highest-risk state, Vermont is the correct choice.",
  "option_label": "Open Vermont (VT) risk detail for priority follow-up"
}
